                <pb facs="0289" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/316: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-20T19:00:00-03:00">December 20, 1935—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>300. From Braden. Department’s 178, December 18, noon. Rodriguez Alves, Podestá
                    Costa, Nieto Del Rio, Rivarola, Dawson and I leaving for Asunción tomorrow
                    morning, returning Monday.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d204-f1"/> [Braden.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
